  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (basis recorded as cash). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary funds statement Total column (p7), whose operating + nonoperating expenses (capital outlay 425,598, principal 13,000, interest 5,022) equal the Statement of Activities business-type expenses 614,208 (p2), used as the printed disbursements total; business-type receipts total computed (sales 83,508 + interest 254). Business-type measure: cash (as FY2024; modified cash net position = cash 81,418 + certificates of deposit 10,294). Proprietary cash flows set null as in FY2024 (non-GAAP). Beginning cash not printed (fund balance only). Ending governmental cash = sum of the printed cash lines (p4); certificates of deposit 17,524 as ending_investments. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4, totals equal the government-wide governmental column p1); business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). The only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental (p5) and proprietary (p7) fund statements; proprietary nonoperating lines are marked outside_printed_total against each fund's printed Total operating expenses. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
